Description: Build inside php-src as ext/openswoole (bundled by this fork), on PHP 7.4 to 8.4. configure built OpenSwoole into every PHP, as it tested PHP_SWOOLE (left over from swoole, unset there) instead of PHP_OPENSWOOLE, and the default of --enable-openswoole was "yes"; now only --enable-openswoole builds it, and configure stops when --enable-swoole is given too (same C++ symbols). Drop the option --enable-openssl, which reset PHP_OPENSSL of --with-openssl to "no" so that mysqlnd built without its OpenSSL code (OpenSwoole now uses OpenSSL when PHP is built --with-openssl, as swoole 6.2 does); drop the -std=c++11 that config.m4 appends to CXXFLAGS, which inside php-src applies to every C++ file and overrides the C++17 that ext/intl needs with ICU 75 and newer; include <stdint.h> in swoole_proxy.h (uint8_t unknown with clang 19). For PHP 8.3 and 8.4, which OpenSwoole 4.12 does not support upstream (OpenSwoole 22 and newer changed the API): the new php_url_encode_hash_ex() of 8.3; zend_str_tolower() for php_strtolower(), gone in 8.4; the C stack bounds that PHP 8.3 checks (EG(stack_base), EG(stack_limit)) follow the coroutine stacks, as in swoole 5.1 and newer, so calls inside coroutines no longer fail with "Maximum call stack size reached"; as 8.4 made exit a function (no ZEND_EXIT opcode), the function exit() is wrapped the way the opcode was, so exit in a coroutine or a server still throws Swoole\ExitException; and the embedded PHP library declares its nullable parameters explicitly (?int, ?array), which PHP 8.4 asks for with a deprecation notice at every start; and the two C++ header checks of configure (valgrind, boost stacktrace) use AC_LANG_PUSH/POP instead of AC_LANG([C++]), which left configure in C++ for every extension after it: their checks ran as C++, and for example readline was not found. On FreeBSD, thirdparty/hiredis/fmacros.h no longer defines _XOPEN_SOURCE and _POSIX_C_SOURCE: they hide the BSD types (u_int32_t) that <netinet/ip6.h> needs, which hiredis/net.c includes through swoole_socket.h, and the build stopped there.
Origin: azsupport

--- a/config.m4
+++ b/config.m4
@@ -31,10 +31,10 @@
